<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chigils</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chigils were a Turkic tribe of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, recorded by Muslim geographers from the 10th century around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/issyk-kul">Lake Issyk-Kul</a> and the upper Chu valley. Closely linked to the Karluk confederation, they were one of the main tribal groups behind the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kara-khanid-khanate">Kara-Khanid Khanate</a> and supplied much of its army. Mahmud al-Kashgari described their dialect in his 11th-century dictionary of the Turkic languages.</p></div>
